# Cache policy for reperi.in (Cloudflare Pages)
#
# Flutter web does NOT hash its file names: main.dart.js, flutter_bootstrap.js,
# assets/* etc. keep the same name on every build. Caching them "immutable"
# for a year meant browsers kept OLD app code after a deploy and mixed it with
# the NEW bootstrap -> blank screen.
#
# "no-cache" does NOT mean "download every time": the browser keeps its copy
# and just asks Cloudflare "has this changed?" (ETag). Unchanged files come
# back as a tiny 304, so it stays fast but is never stale.
#
# Keep this as ONE Cache-Control rule. Cloudflare Pages merges headers from
# every rule that matches a path, so overlapping rules produce conflicting
# Cache-Control values. (The rule below only sets Content-Type, so it merges
# cleanly with this one.)

/*
  Cache-Control: no-cache

# iOS reads this file (no extension) to let the app open reperi.in/community
# links; Apple expects it served as JSON.
/.well-known/apple-app-site-association
  Content-Type: application/json

# Staff-only pages: keep them out of Google search results. (Only adds an
# X-Robots-Tag, so it merges cleanly with the Cache-Control rule above.)
/crm.html
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex, nofollow
/crm-api/*
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex, nofollow
/delivery.html
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex, nofollow
/deliverydashboard.html
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex, nofollow
/washerdashboard.html
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex, nofollow
/washerlogin.html
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex, nofollow
/delete-account.html
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex
